  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a hotel owner positioning in the Caribbean and Latin America around **differentiated guest experience** and **local character**, the strongest lifestyle-oriented brands to consider are **Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, The Luxury Collection, Edition, Six Senses, Vignette Collection, and Moxy**. These brands are either explicitly positioned around local authenticity, design-led lifestyle, or distinctive, experience-driven stays in the region.[5][6]\n\nThe best-supported options from the search results are:\n\n| Brand | Why it fits a lifestyle / local-character positioning | Regional evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Kimpton** | Strong lifestyle brand with design-forward, experiential positioning; part of IHG’s Luxury & Lifestyle set in MLAC | IHG highlights Kimpton in Mexico, Latin America, and the Caribbean, including a forthcoming Kimpton hotel-and-residence in Tulum.[6] |\n| **Hotel Indigo** | Neighborhood- and story-led lifestyle brand, typically built around local culture and place | IHG lists Hotel Indigo in its Luxury & Lifestyle portfolio across MLAC, including Grand Cayman.[6] |\n| **The Luxury Collection** | Highly aligned with destination identity, local heritage, and immersive cultural experiences | Marriott says the brand curates hotels that “reflect the soul of their destinations” with “immense cultural experiences” and “local heritage.”[5][7] |\n| **Edition** | Premium lifestyle brand suited to elevated, design-driven positioning in resort and urban markets | Mentioned in the broader Caribbean/LATAM warm-weather destination set, including Riviera Maya.[4] |\n| **Six Senses** | Strong fit for differentiated, wellness-led, place-based luxury experiences | IHG includes Six Senses in its Luxury & Lifestyle portfolio for MLAC and cites Six Senses La Sagesse Grenada as a 2024 opening.[6] |\n| **Vignette Collection** | Flexible soft-brand style suited to independent character and local storytelling | IHG includes Vignette Collection in MLAC’s Luxury & Lifestyle pipeline.[6] |\n| **Moxy** | If the target is younger, social, playful lifestyle rather than high luxury, Moxy can work well in urban or mixed-use settings | IHG includes Moxy in its broader lifestyle ecosystem globally, though it is not specifically highlighted in the provided regional result.[6] |\n\nA practical way to choose among them:\n\n- **Best for authentic, place-based luxury:** **The Luxury Collection**[5][7]\n- **Best for design-led lifestyle with broad appeal:** **Kimpton** and **Edition**[4][6]\n- **Best for neighborhood storytelling / local texture:** **Hotel Indigo**[6]\n- **Best for wellness and experiential luxury:** **Six Senses**[6]\n- **Best for soft-brand independence with lifestyle positioning:** **Vignette Collection**[6]\n- **Best for younger, more social lifestyle hotels:** **Moxy**\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to:\n- **best brands for beachfront resorts vs. city hotels**\n- **best brands for conversions vs. new builds**\n- **best brands by segment: upper-upscale, luxury, or soft-brand**",
